WEBVTT

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.400
He kept a small light in a chest

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.900
For longer than a life should hold

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.300
He set it in my open hands

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:33.100
And said his watching could be done

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.700
I carried someone through the dark

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.300
Into a hall that knew their step

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:44.000
They pressed a warmth against my chest

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.400
And said the distance wouldn't win

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:53.000
If the road is mine to finish

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.600
Let it finish in the light

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.200
If they offer me a kingdom

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:07.500
I will ask them for the road

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.200
The hall was warm. I faced the door.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.800
The open land still knew my name.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.900
A crown was shining on the stair.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:49.900
I left it with the morning there.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:53.300
If the road is mine to finish

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.800
Let it finish in the light

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.300
If they offer me a kingdom

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:08.800
I will ask them for the road

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.600
At the gate a voice came running

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.800
Asked to match me step for step

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.600
I nodded, and the road grew wider

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.200
Two shadows, one direction

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:42.000
We can leave the lamps behind us

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.700
We can leave the offered throne

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:48.900
If a country knows my name

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:56.000
We'll find it walking, not alone
